<title>USA: Ultramar Diamond cuts posted crude 50 cts.</title>
<headline>Ultramar Diamond cuts posted crude 50 cts.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ultramar Diamond Shamrock said Wednesday that it had lowered the price it will pay for U.S. crude oil by 50 cents a barrel, effective Wednesday.</p>
<p>The decrease brings the new price for U.S. benchmark grade West Texas Intermediate to $16.75 a barrel and Oklahoma Sweet to $16.25.</p>
<p>--New York Energy Desk, +1 212 859 1620</p>
</text>
